This project is based on my Python version of the classic card game War, where I used object-oriented programming (OOP) concepts with classes such as Card, Deck, and Player.
Each class handled part of the game logic — for example:

Card defined the rank, suit, and value of a playing card

Deck created and shuffled all 52 cards

Player managed each player’s deck and card actions

Later, I recreated the same logic in JavaScript to make it interactive and visual in a web browser.
The web version shows cards flipping, players competing, and “WAR” rounds with smooth animations.

Features:

Class-based Python logic converted to JavaScript

Shuffling and dealing of cards

Animated card flips for each round

“WAR” condition handled automatically

Buttons for Start, Step, Auto Play, and Reset

How to use:

Download or clone this project

Open war_game.html in your browser

Click “Start Game” and enjoy the animated version of your Python program
